questions.text:
Consider the following two threads [latex]\mathrm{T} 1 [/latex] and [latex]\mathrm{T} 2 [/latex] that update two shared variables [latex]\mathrm{a} [/latex] and [latex]\mathrm{b} [/latex]. Assume that initially [latex]\mathrm{a}=\mathrm{b}=1 [/latex]. Though context switching between threads can happen at any time, each statement of [latex]\mathrm{T} 1 [/latex] or [latex]\mathrm{T} 2 [/latex] is executed atomically without interruption.<br><br>
[latex]
\begin{array}{cc}
\mathrm{T} 1 & \mathrm{~T} 2 \\
\mathrm{a}=\mathrm{a}+1 ; & \mathrm{b}=2*\mathrm{b} ; \\
\mathrm{b}=\mathrm{b}+1 ; & \mathrm{a}=2*\mathrm{a} ;
\end{array}
 [/latex]
<br><br>
Which one of the following options lists all the possible combinations of values of [latex]\mathrm{a} [/latex] and [latex]\mathrm{b} [/latex] after both [latex]\mathrm{T} 1 [/latex] and [latex]\mathrm{T} 2 [/latex] finish execution?
